  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 AM MDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\n\nThursday, another dry day is expected. The only change is that it \nmay be a degree or two warm on Thursday as compared to today. Friday \nwill be ditto to Thursday, with maybe another 1 degree or two \nincrease in temperatures.\n\nSaturday, the main change this day will be in the mountains. As for \nthe plains. Saturday will be nearly identical to Friday. However, \nover the higher terrain, more clouds are anticipate and there will \nbe a better chance of showers over the Divide, and likewise, temps \nwill be several degrees cooler over the higher terrain. \n\nOn the large scale, the pattern over the region will change as flow \naloft will shift to a southwesterly direction through most of the \ncolumn as a strong trough moves into the northwestern CONUS and \nbegins o dig southward down the Pacific coast.\n\nBy midday Sunday, the trough over the west coast becomes a full \nlongitude trough along the entire coast as aa the main Pacific trough \ninteracts/merges with tropical cyclone activity off the Mexican \ncoast. Flow over the entire Rocky mountain region becomes south-\nsouthwesterly and increases. This will push moisture up into the \nregion and expect quite a few showers to be occurring over the \nContdvd region on this day. This is clearly reflected in the \nstatistical guidance as point forecast for the Wolf Creek region \nshows heavy rain occurring during the latter Sunday/Monday period \nover the Southwest mountains. The plains on this period will likely \nremain dry, but temps are expected to cool into the upper 70s to \nlower 80s across the lower terrain.\n\nFrom Monday into next week, there is still quite a bit of \nuncertainty on the track, speed, flow orientation and moisture with \nthis large scale trough. Although all of the long range \ndeterministic guidance shows the trough moving through during the \nmid week period, there is still lofts of uncertainty. As mentioned \nyesterday, confidence is high that it will be getting cooler over \nthe entire region next week and it will be wet over the CONTDVD \nregion, but how cool and wet (white) still need to be determined. \n\nBased on the latest deterministic guidance, the trough should move \nacross the state later on Wednesday. \\/Hodanish",
